's often just as fast."],"common_mistakes":["Overstriding downhill","Chasing road pace on rough terrain"],"regressions":["Hiking","Running"],"progressions":[],"safety":"Tell someone your route, carry water, and watch for roots and rocks.","video":null,"diagram":"","notes":""},{"id":"ropealt","name":"Alternate-foot jump rope","aliases":["Running step","Jogging step","Alternate foot step"],"training_type":"Cardio","tags":["Cardio","Endurance","Home-friendly"],"muscle_group":"Cardio","primary_muscles":["Calves","Hip flexors"],"secondary_muscles":["Quadriceps","Shoulders","Heart and lungs"],"movement_pattern":"Locomotion","equipment":["Jump rope"],"req":"jumprope","equipment_tier":1,"difficulty":"Intermediate","tracking":"time","unilateral":false,"sets":3,"reps":"1 min","form_cues":["Jog in place, one foot per rope turn.","Keep the knees low and the steps light.","Turn the rope from the wrists."],"common_mistakes":["Lifting the knees too high and catching the rope","Rushing the rope speed"],"regressions":["Boxer skip"],"progressions":["High-knee jump rope"],"safety":"Wear supportive shoes and build up time gradually.","video":null,"diagram":"","notes":""},{"id":"ropeboxer","name":"Boxer skip","aliases":["Boxer step","Boxer shuffle"],"training_type":"Cardio","tags":["Cardio","Combat","Endurance","Home-friendly"],"muscle_group":"Cardio","primary_muscles":["Calves"],"secondary_muscles":["Shoulders","Forearms","Core","Heart and lungs"],"movement_pattern":"Locomotion","equipment":["Jump rope"],"req":"jumprope","equipment_tier":1,"difficulty":"Intermediate","tracking":"time","unilateral":false,"sets":3,"reps":"2 min","form_cues":["Shift your weight side to side, one foot lightly tapping.","Keep the bounce tiny and rhythmic.","Stay relaxed so you can go for full rounds."],"common_mistakes":["Landing on both feet evenly so it's just a basic bounce","Tense shoulders"],"regressions":["Jump rope"],"progressions":["Alternate-foot jump rope","Double unders"],"safety":"Ease in if your calves or Achilles are tight.","video":null,"diagram":"","notes":"Boxers' staple: lets you skip for 3-min rounds with less fatigue."},{"id":"ropecross","name":"Criss-cross jump rope","aliases":["Cross-over","Crossovers"],"training_type":"Cardio","tags":["Cardio","Home-friendly"],"muscle_group":"Cardio","primary_muscles":["Calves","Shoulders"],"secondary_muscles":["Forearms","Chest","Heart and lungs"],"movement_pattern":"Locomotion","equipment":["Jump rope"],"req":"jumprope","equipment_tier":1,"difficulty":"Intermediate","tracking":"count","unilateral":false,"sets":3,"reps":"20–30","form_cues":["Cross your arms at the waist on every second turn.","Push your hands past your hips when crossed.","Jump slightly higher on the crossing turn."],"common_mistakes":["Crossing the arms too high at the chest","Hands not wide enough so the loop is too small"],"regressions":["Jump rope"],"progressions":["Double unders"],"safety":"Use a slightly longer rope while learning.","video":null,"diagram":"","notes":""},{"id":"doubleunder","name":"Double unders","aliases":["DUs","Double jumps"],"training_type":"Cardio","tags":["Cardio","Plyometric","Power"],"muscle_group":"Cardio","primary_muscles":["Calves"],"secondary_muscles":["Shoulders","Forearms","Core","Heart and lungs"],"movement_pattern":"Locomotion","equipment":["Jump rope"],"req":"jumprope","equipment_tier":1,"difficulty":"Advanced","tracking":"count","unilateral":false,"sets":5,"reps":"20–50","form_cues":["Jump a little higher with straight, tight legs.","Flick the wrists hard so the rope passes twice.","Keep elbows in and hands at hip height."],"common_mistakes":["Piking or kicking the feet back","Swinging the arms wide","Jumping far too high"],"regressions":["Jump rope","Criss-cross jump rope"],"progressions":[],"safety":"Use a speed rope and expect whipped shins while learning.","video":null,"diagram":"","notes":"Practise with single-double-single combinations."}]$ex$::jsonb)
